From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Feickert <matthew.feickert@cern.ch>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:37:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Do not add -stdlib=libstdc++ when MathLink is not found

The MathLink check is tried a second time with -stdlib=libstdc++, and the
loop only stops early if the compile works. Without MathLink both
attempts fail, so CONF_STDCPP is left as -stdlib=libstdc++ and is
written to CXXFLAGS and from there to the installed fcc. With clang on
macOS this overrides a -stdlib=libc++ from the environment and asks for
a C++ standard library that is not there.
---
 configure | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 3c56eb0..96e4642 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -391,6 +391,7 @@ _EOF_
   } || {
     echo "no" 1>&3
     CONF_ML=0
+    CONF_STDCPP=
   }
 }
 
